Hi [~accountid:712020:71558a29-6aa8-4ba9-a65c-35de451da5e6] - hope you are well!


I am getting back from holidays and have found this project which requires privacy support. 

I will be able to have a closer look next week on Monday as an urgent priority but on surface this looks like something that does not involve personal data sharing. Can you please clarify for me how we can be excahnging personal data with SumUp?

Per the contract that is attached, the following is indicated:

*Privacy clause - SumUp*

{{SumUp and the Merchant will not share regular personal data under this Agreement.}}
{{In the limited cases where the Merchant may be provided with personal data of the Registered SumUp Merchant}}
{{Accounts, the Merchant guarantees that all Registered SumUp Merchant Accounts falling explicitly}}
{{within the stated scope of the Agreement are informed about such personal data sharing and that}}
{{the data sharing is strictly necessary for the Merchant.}}

It would be helpful if you could clarify what such limited circumstances can be - looking forward to your clarifications! Based on the real data protection risk, we can decide to proceed as is, suggest a short boilerplate clause, or suggest to sign a more detailed Data Sharing/Processing Agreement (seems unlikely so far).

