Hi [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] 

{color:#0747a6}My feedback in blue: {color}

* Schedule 6 section 6 (contractual penalties, can we have penalties under South African law ? Are we ok with such wording or do we need to have liquidated damages concept ?) {color:#0747a6}Yes contractual penalties are permitted in South African law. It will be simpler to keep this clause as is, rather than switch to liquidated damages and need to calculate a genuine pre-estimate of loss. Note that contractual penalties are governed by the Conventional Penalties Act, 1962 - essentially just ensure that the amount is reasonable and proportionate or a Court may reduce should enforcement become litigious. {color}
* Schedule 6 section 7, 8 (check changes in pricing, payment) 
{color:#0747a6}Clause 8.5: Recommend changing the wording slightly - I am concerned that the wording “deemed applicable” is vague where VAT is either chargeable or not. Please see my suggested amendment in the document {color}
* Schedule 6 section 10 (liability charges) - Are we ok with such wording? {color:#0747a6}Yes{color}
* Schedule 7 section 3 (service credits and bonuses but we need CS decision about the amount) {color:#0747a6}- this wording is fine and shouldn't cause issues in SA.{color}

