External legal assessment completed. 

Summary below

Based on the analysis and taking into account the regulatory environment in Poland, my understanding is that there are 2 options for launching Bolt Lux in Poland where Bolt Lux acts as an intermediary:

# Launching as a separate category within Bolt App (similarly as the Premium Category), within the existing intermediary license held by Bolt Rides PL.
## In this case the vehicles would need to operate as taxis, i.e. would need to be marked in accordance with the city regulations and have the taxi lamps;
## Most probably Bolt Lux prices would exceed the maximal prices allowed in accordance with the city regulations so they would need to be classified as some additional services (to the provision of transportation service) - to be discussed with local ops, tax and billing;
# Launching as a separate service, under a separate legal entity with a separate license for intermediation services.
## In this case the services would be provided by the vehicles structurally designed to carry more than 7 and no more than 9 people including the driver (“*Vehicles 7-9pax*”) *and not by taxis,* which means that the Vehicles 7-9pax would not need to comply with the city regulations regarding the markings;
## This model would require cooperation with the fleet partners holding a different license type, i.e. a license for transport of more than 7 and no more than 9 people including the driver, in addition to or instead of the  license for taxi transport for no more than 7 people including the driver (license that the fleets cooperating with Bolt currently hold). This should be explored from the operational side if there are credible partners on the market (1) holding this license or (2) they are willing to apply for it and expand their fleet with new (bigger) vehicles for the purpose of cooperation with Bolt Lux;
## As transportation services with Vehicles 7-9pax was rather designed for occasional transport of people by minivan, and the taxi services are more appropriate for the services that Bolt Lux would provide, there is a risk of authorities challenging this Bolt Lux operating model. It is recommended that if this operating model is pursued, it is done via a separate legal entity, to mitigate the risk for core business in Poland conducted by Bolt Rides PL.
